      "recordId": "CAV2-D52",
      "label": "artifact durability",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "Artifact durability is the axis that classifies a `CAV2-D51` canonical artifact by **intended lifespan** — `ephemeral` (a work-product meant to be produced, consumed, and retired) or `perennial` (a standing reference meant to endure and be maintained). Durability is **orthogonal** to the `authority_kind` (`CAV2-D49`) and to maturity/status (`CAV2-D23`): two artifacts of the same kind may differ in durability — a discovery and an inventory index are both `Evidence`, yet the discovery is ephemeral and the index is perennial. Durability carries one **contradiction-tolerance** obligation (typed coupling, `CAV2-D16`): - an **ephemeral** artifact **may hold live contradictions** — competing hypotheses and unresolved tensions are expected and preserved; - a **perennial** artifact **must not hold live simultaneous contradictions**. *Temporal supersession* — a later entry overriding an earlier one in an append-only record (`CAV2-D26` ledger), or a decision record narrating the contradiction it resolved (`CAV2-D36`) — is **not** a live contradiction and is permitted.",
