      "recordId": "CAV2-D48",
      "label": "authority promotion lifecycle",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "Authority promotion lifecycle is the single staged path by which any authority-bearing candidate may acquire authority — `source evidence -> candidate -> owner-routed review -> promoted authority -> (optional) invariant/constitution pressure` — with per-stage gates, an owner route, and a stopping/demotion rule. It is the generalization that `../promotion-policy.md`'s ladder instantiates and that `CAV2-D43` (patterns), `CAV2-D46` (experience), and the Arcanum Discipline Growth Rule (disciplines) are instances of. When an authority-bearing candidate originates in a domain and is proposed as reusable CAV2 authority, the minimum generalization path is: ```text domain-owned source or candidate -> originating-domain exercise and evidence -> CAV2 import candidate -> generalized proposal with changes and residue stated -> exercise in another independently owned domain or materially distinct context -> challenge and contrary-evidence review -> CAV2 owner decision -> promoted, versioned CAV2 authority -> separate adoption by each domain that chooses to use that version ``` This branch applies to domain-originated definitions, rules, methods, specifications, knowledge structures, validators, and patterns proposed for CAV2-wide reuse only through an existing authority kind and its owner route. Proof objects, Lean results, Cedar or Datalog results, tests, observations, and receipts may support such a candidate as evidence; they do not self-promote.",
