      "recordId": "CAV2-D58",
      "label": "constitution",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "A constitution is an **owner-scoped, selector-bound, composable authority artifact** that turns axioms and invariants into reusable governance rules and policies for named kinds of governed subject. Those subjects may be artifacts, tasks or workflows, repository-owned agent actions, system operations or state transitions, validation surfaces, or authority movements. A constitution must declare its scope, subject kinds, selectors, owner route, authority level, rules and policies, precedence and composition behavior, validation modes or bindings, downstream effect, challenge route, and retirement or split conditions. It constrains a subject only after an owner decision adopts the exact constitution version and scope and the subject matches its selectors. A candidate, selected, or context-loaded constitution does not govern by those facts alone.",
