      "label": "experiment",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "An experiment is a bounded, attributable empirical test that produces observations by applying a declared protocol to a defined subject under named conditions in order to test a question, hypothesis, Goal condition, or Research question. An Experiment artifact must preserve its Project and Goal links, Research links when present, question or hypothesis, subject, protocol, conditions, variables or interventions, measures, environment, prerequisites, stop rules, run references, evidence references, findings references, limitations, owner route, and challenge route. Missing run evidence means the experiment was not shown to have run.",
