      "label": "gate",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "A gate is an explicit checkpoint that decides or routes whether a candidate term, rule, artifact, relation, method, claim, mutation, or execution may continue, must continue with named risk, must stop, or must defer to another owner. Every CyberAlchemy v2 gate must declare its owner route, scope, inputs, criteria, possible verdicts, required evidence, residue handling, record location, and downstream effect. Unless a narrower gate defines otherwise, the minimum verdict vocabulary is `pass`, `flag`, `block`, and `defer`.",
