      "recordId": "CAV2-D59",
      "label": "goal",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "A goal is a durable, attributable statement of a desired future outcome for one project. It says what should become true, why that outcome matters, what is in and out of scope, who owns the goal, how success will be judged, which evidence is required, how it connects to a product thesis or other purpose, and how it can be revised, challenged, achieved, abandoned, or superseded. A goal may stay active without a deadline. It becomes achieved only when its declared success conditions have adequate evidence and the goal owner records the lifecycle change. Activity, progress, a passing sub-check, or an agent claim does not achieve it automatically.",
