      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "A governed artifact tree is a load-bearing artifact tree that exposes the governance interface required before its contents can promote knowledge, constrain future work, or become a reusable authority surface. At minimum, the tree must declare: - owner route - canonical source or source boundary - view roles - evidence inputs - promotion path - validation surface - challenge contract - drift route - allowed uses and blocked uses The tree makes a concept inspectable. It does not make the concept authoritative by itself. Authority still requires the relevant owner route, gate, evidence, and promotion decision.",
