      "label": "intent",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "Intent is the declared purpose, desired capability, problem pressure, or change direction that orients a CyberAlchemy v2 method before the exact output shape, artifact, gate, or implementation path is fully settled. Intent must be attributable, bounded enough to route, revisable under discovery, and traceable to the artifacts, decisions, residue, or next routes that claim to satisfy it. An intent may be refined, split, renamed, or rejected, but it must not be silently replaced by an artifact or implementation convenience.",
