      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "An ontology is a governed meaning layer that represents a domain, workspace, system, or operation as typed knowledge objects, typed relations, branch or role assignments, provenance, confidence, promotion state, and use obligations. In CyberAlchemy v2, an ontology becomes actionable only when it records: - scope or domain of meaning - knowledge object types - typed relations or edge rules - branch, role, or ownership assignment - evidence and provenance references - evidence confidence and commitment confidence when claims are load-bearing - promotion state and next gate - contradiction, drift, residue, or invalidation route - retrieval or use guidance for downstream agents or humans",
