      "recordId": "CAV2-D22",
      "label": "orthogonal classification",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "Orthogonal classification is the CyberAlchemy v2 rule that a governed classification axis, taxonomy label, or ontology grouping is admissible only when it contributes a distinction that is not silently redundant with an existing axis, label, owner lane, lifecycle state, schema field, or typed relation. A classification is orthogonal when changing it does not secretly change a different authority axis. If a proposed classification cannot stay independent, its dependency must be represented through `CAV2-D16` typed coupling invariant before it can govern downstream work.",
