      "label": "primitive type",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "A primitive type is a CyberAlchemy v2 base semantic kind that lower definitions, methods, constitutions, disciplines, schemas, ontology records, or execution artifacts may reference without deriving its meaning from a narrower source space, implementation layer, project glossary, or generated representation. To count as a primitive type, the term must declare its stable name, authority scope, allowed consumers, source-evidence boundary, relation to any external authority term, and the condition under which lower layers may specialize it. Lower layers may instantiate, specialize, or compose a primitive type, but they must not silently redefine it.",
