      "label": "provenance-first navigation",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "Provenance-first navigation is the CyberAlchemy v2 search method that begins from governed entrypoints, constitutions, definition indexes, inventory cards, source manifests, and graph/index surfaces before opening broad conversation, session, or raw source material. Sessions and raw exploratory files may explain why a decision emerged, but they must not be treated as the first or only authority surface when indexed provenance, canonical sources, or owner-authored read models exist.",
