      "label": "residue",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "Residue is the typed remainder exposed by a transformation, translation, promotion, validation, or governance operation when the target representation, layer, or decision path does not preserve, name, justify, validate, or carry all source structure required by the operation's intended use. A residue becomes actionable in CyberAlchemy v2 only when it records: - source operation or transformation - expected preservation or closure condition - observed remainder or failure-locus - residue type - evidence reference - owner route - treatment: repair, type, gate, climb, accept, or defer",
