      "label": "UX/UI knowledge governance",
      "status": "active",
      "meaning": "UX/UI knowledge governance is the CyberAlchemy v2 lens-specific governance interface that turns interface iteration, browser evidence, accessibility evidence, visual evidence, interaction traces, user-study residue, and reusable experience lessons into governed candidates without treating subjective experience quality as automatic authority. It must separate at least these lanes: - captured interface lesson - reusable UX/UI pattern candidate - browser-observable evidence - accessibility and semantic evidence - layout and interaction evidence - cognitive or attention risk proxy - domain-practice heuristic - human-study or expert-review residue - promotion request and owner decision UX/UI knowledge governance can produce candidate lessons, patterns, claim maps, validator specs, fixture plans, studio annotation intents, evidence reports, and promotion requests. It does not promote UX/UI authority by itself.",
